<title>SWEDEN: Swedish public debt down to 77.7 pct of GDP.</title>
<headline>Swedish public debt down to 77.7 pct of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's public sector debt fell to 77.7 percent of Gross Domestic Product in 1996, from 78.2 percent in 1995, the Swedish news agency TT on Tuesday quoted a finance ministry source as saying.</p>
<p>The government, in its 1997 budget proposals, had predicted 1996 debt equal to 78.1 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>Sweden is yet to decide if it will join the European Union's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>Membership criteria state that a country's gross government debt should be a maximum 60 percent of GDP or approaching that level at a &quot;satisfactory pace&quot;.</p>
<p>--Stockholm newsroom +46 8 7001003</p>
